 "comment": "Scenarios for the Drive sync engine (S4b-BL-118, docs/15 \u00a75.1). Run by Kotlin DriveSyncScenariosTest and web drive-sync-scenarios.spec.ts over a fake Drive and the real encryption core. Devices are named; each has a key; ids are random, so no scenario depends on a tie between two devices' ids (an advance separates conflicting edits). Steps: edit/delete (a house), advance (the fake clock), skew (a device's clock offset), sync (device, optional confirm/stale/force, expect: kind, wrote, held, take, skipped (sorted reasons), housesToDelete, liveHouses; expectError: a DriveException kind), expectLabels (all houses of a device), expectLabel, expectDirty, failDrive/healDrive (op UPDATE with a 5xx status, or ALL with status 0 = offline), corruptNextDownload, plant (a file in a slot: copy, flip, plain), expectPlantsKept, revoke, snapshot/replay/trashLastFile.",
